An opioid-continuation may initiate a long-term-opioid-therapy after 30 days.
If a clinician does not make an intentional-benefit-risk-decision with a patient then the clinician should not initiate a long-term-opioid-therapy.
If a clinician does not conduct an informed-discussion with a patient then the clinician should not initiate a long-term-opioid-therapy.
If a clinician does not use a comprehensive-pain-management then the clinician should not initiate a long-term-opioid-therapy.
